; ============================================================================
; DNS for AI Discovery (DNS-AID) zone file for PRISM Benchmark
; ============================================================================
; Reference: draft-mozleywilliams-dnsop-dnsaid-02
;   https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-mozleywilliams-dnsop-dnsaid/
; RFC 9460: Service Binding and Parameter Specification via the DNS (SVCB)
;   https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9460
;
; STATUS: DOCUMENTATION ONLY -- not authoritative
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The current site is served from prism-benchmark.github.io, a subdomain of
; github.io that is owned and operated by GitHub. The PRISM maintainers do
; NOT control the github.io zone, so these SVCB records cannot be published
; from this repository and the live DNS-AID check at isitagentready.com will
; continue to report "DNS-AID records not found" until the project migrates
; to a custom domain.
;
; To activate, replace `prism-benchmark.github.io` with the new apex (e.g.
; prism-benchmark.org) and publish the records at the registrar. Sign the
; zone with DNSSEC per the security considerations in section 6 of the
; draft; if you later add TLSA records, DNSSEC signing is REQUIRED.
;
; Capability descriptor and integrity digest
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The agent's capability descriptor is published at
; /.well-known/agent-card.json (relative to the apex). The base64url-encoded
; SHA-256 digest of its canonical form is embedded below in the `cap-sha256`
; SvcParamKey so consumers can verify the descriptor on every fetch.
;
; Canonical-form definition (matches the format produced by Python's
; json.dumps with sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":") and ensure_ascii=False;
; equivalent to RFC 8785 JCS for this document):
;   - Object keys sorted lexicographically at every level
;   - No insignificant whitespace
;   - UTF-8, NFC-normalized, no trailing newline
;
; Recompute with:
;   python3 -c "import json,hashlib,base64; \
;     d=hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(json.load(open('public/.well-known/agent-card.json')), \
;     sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'), ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')).digest(); \
;     print(d.hex()); print(base64.urlsafe_b64encode(d).rstrip(b'=').decode())"
;
; Current canonical-form digest (hex):
;   cbed001dedad08098c06cc527ebddcc434de2a3876af1b3cf0460fddfc3ba8a1
; Current canonical-form digest (base64url):
;   y-0AHe2tCAmMBsxSfr3cxDTeKjh2rxs88EYP3fw7qKE

$ORIGIN prism-benchmark.github.io.
$TTL    3600

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Apex HTTPS binding (RFC 9460, Section 9)
; Advertises the apex origin as an HTTPS endpoint so clients can skip the
; A/AAAA round trip and learn supported ALPN protocols up front. Used here
; as the ServiceMode form (SvcPriority 1) with TargetName "." meaning the
; owner name of the record is the effective TargetName.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
prism-benchmark.github.io.  3600  IN  HTTPS  1 . (
    alpn="h2,h3"
    port=443
    ipv4hint=185.199.108.153
    ipv4hint=185.199.109.153
    ipv4hint=185.199.110.153
    ipv4hint=185.199.111.153
    ipv6hint=2620:112:3000:1a81::1
    ipv6hint=2620:112:3000:1a82::1
    ipv6hint=2620:112:3000:1a83::1
    ipv6hint=2620:112:3000:1a84::1
)

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; A2A agent endpoint  (DNS-SD service label _a2a._agents.<apex>)
; Per draft-mozleywilliams-dnsop-dnsaid Section 3.1, this is the primary
; record an AI agent client queries when it knows both the organization
; and the agent. The `well-known` and `cap` parameters let the client
; resolve the capability descriptor published at the same origin and
; `cap-sha256` lets it verify the descriptor on every fetch.
;
; `mandatory` lists the keys a consumer MUST understand and apply, so that
; an attacker on the path cannot downgrade by stripping them.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
_a2a._agents.prism-benchmark.github.io.  3600  IN  SVCB  1 . (
    alpn="a2a,h2"
    port=443
    ipv4hint=185.199.108.153
    ipv6hint=2620:112:3000:1a81::1
    well-known="agent-card.json"
    cap="https://prism-benchmark.github.io/prism-page/.well-known/agent-card.json"
    cap-sha256="y-0AHe2tCAmMBsxSfr3cxDTeKjh2rxs88EYP3fw7qKE"
    mandatory="alpn,port,cap-sha256"
)

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Organization agent index  (DNS-SD service label _index._agents.<apex>)
; Per draft-mozleywilliams-dnsop-dnsaid Section 3.2, an AI client that
; knows the organization but not the specific agent starts here. The
; TargetName points at the same index document published via the .well-known
; path; downstream consumers perform semantic search over the listed agents.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
_index._agents.prism-benchmark.github.io.  3600  IN  SVCB  1 . (
    alpn="h2"
    port=443
    ipv4hint=185.199.108.153
    ipv6hint=2620:112:3000:1a81::1
    well-known="agent-card.json"
    cap="https://prism-benchmark.github.io/prism-page/.well-known/agent-card.json"
    cap-sha256="y-0AHe2tCAmMBsxSfr3cxDTeKjh2rxs88EYP3fw7qKE"
    mandatory="alpn,port,cap-sha256"
)

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DNSSEC
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The draft recommends that public DNS-AID zones be DNSSEC-signed so that
; validating resolvers can return authenticated data and consumers can
; detect tampering of the SVCB RRset (or any TLSA records that follow).
; Use a registered DS algorithm with broad resolver support and follow the
; operational guidance in RFC 6781. If TLSA records are published at
; _443._tcp.<apex> to support DANE TLS authentication (RFC 6698 / RFC 7671),
; DNSSEC signing of this zone is REQUIRED by the draft.
;
; Optional: TLSA records at _443._tcp.prism-benchmark.github.io for
; permissive DANE posture (3 1 1 <sha256 of SPKI>). Not included here
; because the certificate material is controlled by the apex operator.
